        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Frank Ocean, Matt Martians\n- Organizations: ASAP Mob, Odd Future, Pro Era, Flatbush Zombies\n- Products: Cozy Tapes Vol. 2: Too Cozy, \"Swim Good\", Nostalgia, Ultra\n- Groups: The Jet Age of Tomorrow, The Super D3Shay, The Internet, Sweaty Martians\n\nFacts:\n- In 2010, Frank Ocean became a member of the hip hop collective Odd Future.\n- In 2011, \"Swim Good\" was released as the second single from Frank Ocean's mixtape Nostalgia, Ultra.\n- Frank Ocean, born Christopher Edwin Breaux on October 28, 1987, is an American singer and songwriter.\n- Frank Ocean is known for an idiosyncratic musical style and first worked as a ghostwriter.\n- Matt Martians was a founding member of the Los Angeles hip hop collective Odd Future.\n- Matt Martians is part of The Jet Age of Tomorrow with Pyramid Vritra, The Super D3Shay with Pyramid Vritra and brandUn DeShay, The Internet with Syd, and Sweaty Martians with Earl Sweatshirt.\n- Cozy Tapes Vol. 2: Too Cozy is the second studio album by the American hip hop collective ASAP Mob.\n- Cozy Tapes Vol. 2: Too Cozy features guest appearances from Big Sean, Playboi Carti, Pro Era, Quavo, Lil Uzi Vert, Lil Yachty, Chief Keef, Gucci Mane, Schoolboy Q, Frank Ocean, Jaden Smith, Smooky Margielaa, and Flatbush Zombies.",
